Purpose: Deny stock chrome:// WebUI by default: remove every non-Corvid chrome:// WebUIConfig after Chromium registers them. Navigations are redirected/blocked earlier by the URL handler from 0200 (corvid::StockPagePolicy).
Area: ui
Files: chrome/browser/ui/webui/chrome_web_ui_configs.cc (end of RegisterChromeWebUIConfigs)
Rebase risk: low because it is one call at the end of a function; the removal logic lives in the overlay
Origin: original (written for Corvid; no third-party patch text reused)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/chrome_web_ui_configs.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/chrome_web_ui_configs.cc
index 559dd66734ec..75c33ba9d164 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/chrome_web_ui_configs.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/chrome_web_ui_configs.cc
@@ -520,4 +520,7 @@ void RegisterChromeWebUIConfigs() {
   map.AddWebUIConfig(std::make_unique<skills::SkillsUIConfig>());
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || \
         // BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
+
+  // Drop every stock chrome:// WebUI (deny by default).
+  corvid::RemoveStockWebUIConfigs();
 }
